3. Now go to the /var/named directory
# cp -p named.localhost forward.zone
# cp -p named.loopback reverse.zone
# vim forward.zone
do this entries
$TTL 1D
@       IN SOA  DNS-server.example.com.         root.DNS-server.example.com. (
                                                0       ; serial
                                                1D      ; refresh
                                                1H      ; retry
                                                1W      ; expire
                                                3H )    ; minimum
                NS      DNS-server.example.com.
DNS-server      A       192.168.159.143
dnsmaster       CNAME   DNS-server

#vim reverse.zone
$TTL 1D
@       IN SOA  DNS-server.example.com.         root.DNS-server.example.com. (
                                                0       ; serial
                                                1D      ; refresh
                                                1H      ; retry
                                                1W      ; expire
                                                3H )    ; minimum
        NS      DNS-server.example.com.
143     PTR     DNS-server.example.com.
146     PTR     DNS-slave.example.com.

4. save the files and then goto the /etc/resolv.conf
# vim /etc/resolv.conf
 nameserver 192.168.159.143     => it should be dns server ip


5. then save the files and then test it
# dig DNS-server.example.com 		 =>  check dig with your hostname with fqdn


after run this command make sure that 

QUERY: 1, ANSWER: 1     => both the values should be 1 if not check the status of named service 

6. Then come to the slave server
	First install the "bind" package into your machine
  	# install bind -y  

7. Do same step-2 which you do in the master and only do changes in zone lines
zone "example.com" IN {
        type slave;
        masters { 192.168.159.143; };
        file "slaves/forward.zone";
};

zone "159.168.192.in-addr.arpa" IN {
        type slave;
        masters { 192.168.159.143; };
        file "slaves/reverse.zone";
};
8. Then do changes in /etc/resolv.conf file 
# vim /etc/resolv.conf
nameserver 192.168.159.143  => master ip 
nameserver 192.168.159.146  => slave ip

9. and then save it and also allow dns service on firewall and test it with dig command 

# firewall-cmd --permanent --add-service=dns
# firewall-cmd --reload

# dig DNS-slave.example.com
and same you will get  QUERY: 1, ANSWER: 1  if not this will showing 1 then test the status of named with systemctl status named.service or with journalctl -xeu named




